Subject: [PATCH 4/5] gdn: split-K GEMM for in_proj_ba at small token counts

For the per-rank in_proj_ba at an MTP K=3 verify step (x[4, 5120] @
W[48, 5120]^T at TP=2) cuBLAS on sm_86 picks a cutlass wmma kernel with a
4-CTA grid: ~28 us idle, ~41 us in-server, x 48 GDN layers per decode step.
A Triton split-K (S=16) takes 6.7 us. The op dispatches only at M <= 16;
larger batches keep F.linear, where cuBLAS is already fast. Unquantized,
bias-free in_proj_ba only (the gate-logit projection is never quantised).

Measured on 2x3090 TP=2: c1 median ITL -1.25 ms at 4K (-5.9 %),
-1.30 ms at 32K (-5.5 %), -1.05 ms at 250K (-3.0 %); flat at c8/c32.
Not bit-identical to cuBLAS: the reduction order differs (fp32 accumulate).

Validated on sm_86 only. On by default. VLLM_GDN_BA_SPLITK=0 disables it;
the knob is a registered envs.py bool, so it is part of the compile cache key.

Proof: "GDN in_proj_ba SPLIT-K ACTIVE: M=.. N=.. K=5120 S=16" once per rank.
